{
 "protocol": "\n    Phase 0 D2 (Yotam 11-28, data only, no model): how much of the swap target x(s, r) is determined by (dry s, RIR r),\n    and how much is per-clip noise? Extends check 3 (room_share.py), which could not separate the noise from the\n    source x room interaction.\n\n    Re-rendering. Every clip of paired v2 is rebuilt exactly as gen_simu_paired.Renderer.render: the dry source (the\n    md5-checked dry tar of check 3; paired v2 has the same seed and utterances as v1, checked here for every utterance) *\n    the stored two-channel RIR and direct-path RIR (<tar>.rirs.npz, x peak), then diffuse white noise at the clip's\n    stored SNR (re the direct path), peak-normalised. Two noise draws per clip: 'a' = the original seed\n    (seed + 2,000,000 + clip id; checked against the stored wav on the first clips), 'b' = an independent seed. Same\n    source, RIR and SNR: only the noise waveform differs.\n\n    Features (the swap loss's STFT and normalisation; ipd16 standardised with C v2's spatial input statistics):\n      frame   per-frame ipd16 channels: log|L|, ILD, cos IPD, sin IPD (the current swap target; IPD weighted per bin\n              by the loss's magnitude weight)\n      seg16   per 16-frame segment (256 ms = one decoder patch column), from the segment-summed spectra:\n              log sum|L|^2, ILD = log sum|R|^2 - log sum|L|^2, cos / sin of the cross-spectrum phase angle(sum L R*),\n              IC = |sum L R*| / sqrt(sum|L|^2 sum|R|^2) (interaural coherence)\n      clip    the same five over the whole clip (256 frames): one value per frequency bin per clip\n    Variance (around each bin's mean over all clips, frames or segments; weighted as above) is split into\n      noise        0.5 E[(f_a - f_b)^2]: what no model can predict, even knowing s and r exactly;\n      room main    from scene groups (500 held-out scenes x their 4 utterances): total - within-scene x k/(k-1);\n      speech main  from utterance groups (500 utterances x their 4 scenes): total - within-utterance x k/(k-1);\n      interaction  the rest (total - room - speech - noise): source x room, needs both encoders.\n    Ceiling = 1 - noise share: the explained variance a decoder that knew s and r exactly could reach.\n    Bands: 0-2 / 2-4 / 4-6 / 6-8 kHz and all.\n\n    Usage: python d2_ceiling.py --out <json> [--n_groups 500]\n",
